Package: riposte
Title: Combined Randomization-Based Tests Across Outcome Representations
Version: 0.0.0.9009
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Jake",
           family = "Bowers",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "jake@jakebowers.org",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4048-1166")),
    person(given = "Myla",
           family = "Burton",
           role = c("aut", "cph")))
Description: Tests of the sharp null of no treatment effects that combine several
    representations of an outcome (raw values, ranks, pairwise mean
    distances, a max distance, and a bounded transform) to detect treatment
    effects a difference of means misses, in completely randomized, block-
    randomized, and cluster-randomized experiments. The package combines the
    representations three ways: a quadratic (energy/distance)
    omnibus that uses the full permutation covariance, a Cauchy combination
    that uses only the marginal calibrations, and a max combination. A screen
    chooses between the quadratic and the Cauchy from the conditioning of the
    permutation covariance, an ancillary quantity. By default, p-values use
    direct re-randomization. Optional chi-square and Cauchy approximations are
    available for unadjusted quadratic and Cauchy tests. The acronym is Randomization
    Inference for Power via Outcome representationS, Tests, and Estimation.
